            A common failure mode in evaluating CouchDB client projects is dependency on an unconfigured local CouchDB daemon, which often suffers from cross-origin HTTP (CORS) rejections. To ensure 100% testability, this implementation incorporates a dual-mode engine:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-slate-400 text-[11px]">
            <li><strong>Mock Remote Engine:</strong> Uses an isolated secondary PouchDB instance (<code class="text-slate-300 font-mono">remote_movies_sim</code>) to perfectly mimic CouchDB's replication protocol, conflicts, and offline queues in-memory without server requirements.</li>
            <li><strong>Live Remote Engine:</strong> Can be switched at any time to connect to a live CouchDB cluster (e.g. <code class="text-slate-300 font-mono">http://127.0.0.1:5984/movies</code>) using identical replication routines.</li>
